// FILE: directory_law_v1.law
/*******************************************************************************
 *                           AVIS.ARTIFACT HEADER
 * TYPE: LAW
 * CLASS: DIRECTORY-LAW
 * NAME: DIRECTORY-LAW-V1
 * VERSION: 1.00
 * ROLE: Filesystem Governance for /mercwar01/
 * ENGINE: AVIS-2026 / AIFVS-MODE
 * ORIGIN: /mercwar01/law/directory_law_v1.law
 *******************************************************************************
 * [PURPOSE]
 * Define the structure, purpose, and rules governing the filesystem under
 * /mercwar01/ to ensure clarity, consistency, and predictable organization.
 *
 * [ROOT STRUCTURE]
 * /mercwar01/
 *   /bin/        → Executable scripts and binaries
 *   /www/        → Web-facing files
 *   /log/        → Logs and output traces
 *   /law/        → Governance artifacts
 *   /modules/    → Functional components
 *   /data/       → Persistent data storage
 *   /tmp/        → Temporary files
 *
 * [DIRECTORY PRINCIPLES]
 * 1. Explicit Placement:
 *    Every artifact must be placed in the correct directory.
 *
 * 2. No Drift:
 *    Files may not be relocated without explicit instruction.
 *
 * 3. Clear Purpose:
 *    Each directory serves a single, well-defined role.
 *
 * 4. Predictable Naming:
 *    Filenames must reflect purpose and scope.
 *
 * [EXTENSION RULES]
 * - New directories must be documented and justified.
 * - Extensions must not conflict with existing structure.
 *
 * [COMPLIANCE]
 * All filesystem operations must follow this law to maintain order and clarity.
 *******************************************************************************
 * [END AVIS.ARTIFACT]
 *******************************************************************************/
